  "intro": "Before 1750 your address in Clifton Hill stood on the basalt plain above Merri Creek, in open woodland of widely spaced River Red Gum and Yellow Box over a deep, flowering grassland of Kangaroo Grass, wallaby grasses, lilies and daisies. Murnong (Yam Daisy) and Chocolate Lilies grew through the tussocks in spring. Very little of this woodland survives across Melbourne's north and west, and it is considered Endangered in this bioregion. The plants below are indigenous to it and grouped by the layer they fill. Keep the trees few and far apart, and give most of the space to the grassland beneath them.",
